# Application

Product logic. Register in `DependencyInjection.AddApplication()`.

**Regions, boundaries, injection naming:** `conventions.mdc`. **Promotion:** `solution.mdc`. **Lifecycle flags:** `infrastructure.mdc`.

```text
Features/       vertical slices + Shared/; domain folders (Dbo/, Chat/, Workspace/)
AI/             ChatOrchestrator, Agents, Tools, Memory, Workflows
Models/         AI turn shapes, ChatMessageRoles
Utilities/      technical cross-cutting only (crypto) — not slice business logic
```

### Helpers vs Utilities

| | `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` or `Shared/Helpers.cs` | `Application/Utilities/` |
|---|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| **What** | Slice or cross-slice **business** logic | **Technical** plumbing with no slice owner |
| **Examples** | `EmailSettingsMapping`, inbox date parsing for AI | `CryptographyHelpers`, `Encrypt()` |
| **Promote** | Handler → slice `Helpers` → `Shared/Helpers` | 2+ slices need same technical helper |

`WebApp/Utilities/` is UI/auth only — not Application business logic.

## Features — vertical slices

| Folder | Repository | Entity |
|--------|------------|--------|
| `Dbo/Users/` | `UserRepository` | `Dbo.User` |
| `Dbo/EmailProviders/` | `EmailProviderRepository` | `Dbo.EmailProvider` |
| `Chat/ChatThreads/` | `ChatThreadRepository` | `Chat.ChatThread` |
| `Chat/ChatMessages/` | `ChatMessageRepository` | `Chat.ChatMessage` |
| `Workspace/EmailAccounts/` | `EmailAccountRepository` | `Workspace.EmailAccount` |
| `Workspace/Contacts/` | `ContactRepository` | `Workspace.Contact` |
| `Workspace/Tags/` | `TagRepository` | `Workspace.Tag` |
| `Workspace/Buckets/` | `BucketRepository` | `Workspace.Bucket` |
| `Shared/` | `SharedRepository`, `Helpers.cs`, `DTOs.cs`, `Services.cs` | — |

```text
Features/{Domain}/{Area}/
  DTOs.cs  Repository.cs  Helpers.cs  Services.cs   (add only when needed)
  Commands/  Queries/
```

Same file names in `{Slice}/` and `Shared/` — multiple types per file; no one-off `*Mapping.cs` files.

**Workspace referables:** `id` = stable FK key; `alias` = per-user unique handle (slugified via `EntityAliasRules`); AI refs (`contact:`, `mailbox:`, …) resolved via `WorkspaceReferenceService` at boundaries only.

**`Dbo.EmailProvider`:** system rows (`IsSystem`, `UserId = null`) read-only for all; custom rows owned by user. List scoped to system + that user's custom rows.

**Deferred:** no server theme/prefs storage until product requires it.

## Data access

- **All EF in repos** — handlers never inject `IDbContextFactory`
- Slice repos: ctor `IDbContextFactory`; each method owns ctx → query/mutate → `SaveChanges`
- `AI/` and `Shared/Services.cs` use slice repos or `SharedRepository` only
- Reads: `{Dto}.FromEntity` / `FromEntities` on `DTOs.cs`
- Writes: repo methods; mapping in `Helpers.cs` only for non-DTO transforms

| Consumer | Single-slice | Cross-slice |
|----------|--------------|-------------|
| Handler | `{Slice}Repository` | `SharedRepository` or second slice repo |
| `AI/`, Shared services | `{Slice}Repository` | `SharedRepository` |

Promote to `SharedRepository` only when query truly spans entity folders.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention |
|------|------------|
| Use case | `{UseCase}Request` / `{UseCase}Response` — not `SignInCommand` |
| Queries | `GetAll{Entity}By{Filter}` · `Get{Entity}ById` · `Get{Entity}For{Purpose}` |
| Commands | `{Verb}{Entity}[{Detail}]` |
| Repo methods | Mirror query verb; no redundant entity prefix (`UpdateProfileAsync` not `UpdateUserProfileAsync`) |
| AI-only repo reads | suffix `ForAI` on method name |
| Request ids | `UserId` first; descriptive ids (`ThreadId`, `EmailAccountId`) — not bare `Id` |
| Chat | `ThreadId` in app code; SQL column stays `ChatThreadId` |

**Use-case file order:** Request → Response → Validator → Handler.

**References:** `Dbo/Users/Commands/SignIn.cs`, `Chat/ChatMessages/Commands/SendChatMessage.cs`, `Workspace/EmailAccounts/`.

## Handlers

1. `var result = new Result<T>();` first line
2. `#region # Execute` + `#region # Handle Result` — see `conventions.mdc`
3. No EF — inject repos only
4. `#region # Private Helpers` for non-DB orchestration only

| Repo param | Name |
|------------|------|
| `UserRepository` | `userRepo` |
| `ChatThreadRepository` | `chatThreadRepo` |
| `ChatMessageRepository` | `chatMessageRepo` |
| `EmailAccountRepository` | `emailAccountRepo` |
| `EmailProviderRepository` | `emailProviderRepo` |
| `ContactRepository` | `contactRepo` |
| `TagRepository` | `tagRepo` |
| `BucketRepository` | `bucketRepo` |
| `SharedRepository` | `sharedRepo` |

FluentValidation max lengths must match EF `HasMaxLength` (source: SQL scripts + `AppDbContext`).

Do **not** put use-case types or slice DTOs in Infrastructure or WebApp.

